# API / commands

`src/api/` is Discord command registry and gateway routing — not an HTTP API.

## Flow

1. `ApiManager` wires `clientReady`, `interactionCreate`, `messageCreate`
2. On ready: `application.commands.set(...)` from `ApiV1.commands`
3. Slash / context menu: name match in `api-v1.ts` → `container.resolve(handler)` → `handle(interaction)`
4. Mentions / replies to bot: `routeMention` → `GrokManager` (not slash routing)

## Adding a command

1. Implement `SlashCommandHandler` in `src/api/routes/*-routes.ts` (`@injectable()` if deps)
2. Register in `ApiV1`: `new SlashCommand(builder, HandlerClass)`
3. Keep handlers thin — domain work belongs in `AudioManager` / `GrokManager` / `ChannelManager`

```typescript
// ✅ thin handler
async handle(interaction: ChatInputCommandInteraction) {
    await interaction.deferReply()
    await this.audioManager.play(/* ... */)
}
```

## Conventions

- Narrow interaction type early; else `throw new BotError(...)`
- Long ops (`/play`, `/draw`, Ask Cyan): `deferReply`; error path must `editReply` when deferred
- User-facing failures: `new BotError('log reason', 'user-visible text')`
- Do not `new` handlers in the router — DI-resolve them
